# DAA Lab 08 — Dynamic Programming

**Course:** Design and Analysis of Algorithms (DAA), Lab-08 · BTech (CS-B and CE), 3rd Semester
**Instructor:** Dr. Ajaya Kumar Dash · **Paper date:** September 29, 2026
**Language:** C (standard C99, tested with GCC) · **Paradigm:** Dynamic Programming

The original question paper is kept unchanged in this folder as [`DAA_LAB_08_QUESTION_PAPER.pdf`](DAA_LAB_08_QUESTION_PAPER.pdf).

---

## 1. Lab Overview
The paper has **9 questions**. Questions 1–8 are classic **dynamic-programming** problems (coin change, LCS, LIS, edit distance, rod cutting, optimal BST). Question 9 is the **Collatz Conjecture**, an *open unsolved problem*, handled as a research-oriented computational investigation (see the [Collatz Research](#collatz-research) section). Every question has its own folder with the exact question, a written algorithm, and a C program. All run results are kept together in `Outputs/`.

## 2. Objectives
* Recognise when a problem has **optimal substructure** and **overlapping subproblems**.
* Define a DP table, write its recurrence, fill it **bottom-up**, and **reconstruct** the actual answer (coins, subsequence, edit operations, cuts, tree).
* Derive time and space complexity from the loops of the algorithm.
* Choose a sensible **input representation** and validate programs with test cases.
* Practise C: arrays, dynamic memory (`malloc`/`calloc`/`realloc`/`free`), functions, overflow handling.
* Experience a simple-looking **open problem** (Collatz) and learn the difference between *experiment* and *proof*.

